Civilization is a large group of people living and working together, representing a unified, common culture of society.
The word "civilization" is related to the Latin words "civis," meaning "citizen," and "civitas," meaning "city" or "city-state," and in some contexts, "society"; it is derived from the Latin word "civilis," which means "civil" or "citizen."
