The Great Pyramid in Giza is one of the seven wonders that still exist today.
The Great Pyramid, built by the Egyptians in the third century BCE, is one of many large pyramid structures constructed in honor of the deceased Pharaoh.
The Giza plateau, also known as the "Giza Necropolis," in the Egyptian desert includes several pyramids (the largest of which is the Great Pyramid), numerous smaller tombs, a number of temples, and the Great Sphinx.
The Great Pyramid was built in honor of the pharaoh Khufu, and numerous smaller pyramids, tombs, and temples were constructed in honor of Khufu's wives and family members.
