Sleep disorder is the process of waking up earlier than your usual sleep time and then falling back asleep within a short time (10–60 minutes).
You can easily achieve this by using a relatively quiet alarm clock that gently wakes you up without startling you.
If you are turning off the clock while you are asleep, you may place it in the other corner of the room, in which case you will have to get up from your seat to turn it off.
